<h1>Comserv Changelog</h1>

<div style="margin:16px 0;padding:12px 16px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary-color,#1565c0);background:var(--bg-secondary,#f5f5f5);">
    <p><strong>Policy (2026-06):</strong> Append <em>all new code changes</em> here — do not create new <code>YYYY-MM-DD-*.tt</code> changelog files.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Code changes</strong> → this file (<code>/Documentation/CHANGELOG</code>)</li>
        <li><strong>Member how-to</strong> → stable <code>Documentation/guides/*.tt</code> (update in place) or <code>page.feature_guide</code></li>
        <li><strong>Pre-2026 per-file history</strong> → read-only archive: <a href="/Documentation/all_changelog">all_changelog</a></li>
        <li><strong>Where to put docs</strong> → <a href="/Documentation/newsletter_feature_guide_workflow">documentation decision guide</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>

<h2>[Unreleased]</h2>
<p><em>Add bullets here while working; move to a dated section when shipped.</em></p>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: Production container can never be deleted by cleanup (recurring 521 outage root cause)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> computersystemconsulting.ca repeatedly returns Cloudflare Error 521 ("web server is down") — the <code>comserv2-web-prod</code> container (or its volumes/networks) was being deleted, almost daily, by blind <code>docker</code> prune/rm paths. The DB container stayed healthy; only the web origin vanished.</li>
    <li><strong>Root cause — three unguarded deletion paths:</strong>
        <ul>
            <li><code>script/docker-cleanup.sh</code> ran a bare <code>docker container prune -f</code> (line 28) — deletes <em>any</em> stopped container, including prod if it ever briefly exits.</li>
            <li><code>script/deploy.sh</code> monitor routine cleanup ran unfiltered <code>docker volume prune -f</code> / <code>docker network prune -f</code> every cron tick — could reap prod's named resources if detached.</li>
            <li>Legacy <code>deploy.sh</code> <code>docker container prune -f --filter "until=1h"</code> (already guarded 2026-08-11) — kept as the safe label filter.</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Fix (<code>script/deploy.sh</code>):</strong> added a PRODUCTION CONTAINER PROTECTION block — <code>is_prod_container()</code>, <code>protect_prod_resources()</code> (labels the live prod container <code>comserv.role=prod</code>), and safe-prune helpers <code>safe_prune_stopped_containers()</code> / <code>safe_prune_volumes()</code> / <code>safe_prune_networks()</code>. Monitor self-heal now calls <code>protect_prod_resources</code>; routine cleanup only prunes stopped containers labeled <code>comserv.prune=safe</code>, dangling volumes, and unused (non-prod) networks. Prod's named volumes/networks are never reaped.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (<code>script/docker-cleanup.sh</code>):</strong> replaced the bare <code>docker container prune -f</code> with the same <code>label=comserv.prune=safe</code> filter and a loud warning if a prod-named container is found stopped (never removed).</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (<code>lib/Comserv/Util/DockerDeploy.pm</code>):</strong> the intentional deploy-time <code>docker rm -f</code> of the live prod container now only runs when a rollback backup image exists; otherwise it is skipped so a failed recreate cannot leave prod permanently down with no restore.</li>
    <li><strong>Net effect:</strong> the production web container, its <code>comserv2_*</code> volumes, and its networks are now NEVER removed by any cleanup path — only an explicit, backup-backed deploy recreates them.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>bash -n</code> clean on both scripts; <code>perl -c</code> clean on DockerDeploy.pm.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Added — 2026-08-15: Logging Audit feature (project #265 LOG-AUDIT)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>What:</strong> in-app logging-coverage audit that enforces the error-audit trail policy (.ai-policy.md §7 / ai-editor-workflow hardblock). Detects (a) system_log error hotspots (grouped by level/area, last 7 days) and (b) code blocks in <code>lib/</code> that swallow errors (eval/catch with die/throw but no <code>log_with_details</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> <code>script/hardware_monitor.pl</code> now also POSTs to <code>/admin/logging_audit/run</code> on the node that answered (same token, same node) — no separate cron needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Endpoints:</strong> <code>/admin/logging_audit/run</code> (token-guarded, cron; added to Root.pm auto-bypass), <code>/admin/logging_audit/trigger</code> (manual, admin-gated), <code>/admin/logging_audit</code> (results page with "Run scan now" button).</li>
    <li><strong>Storage:</strong> new <code>logging_audit</code> table — Result class <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/LoggingAudit.pm</code> is the source of truth; <strong>deploy via schema-compare</strong> (NOT yet deployed).</li>
    <li><strong>Scan logic:</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/LoggingAudit.pm</code> — reports only, never edits code; findings stored per scan run; summary logged via log_with_details.</li>
    <li><strong>UI:</strong> added "Logging Audit" link to admin top menu (admintopmenu.tt) and admin map (admin_map.tt); results page <code>root/admin/LoggingAudit/Index.tt</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Plan doc:</strong> <code>root/Documentation/LOG-AUDIT-PLAN.tt</code> (project #265, parent #258 HWMON).</li>
    <li><strong>Outstanding:</strong> schema-compare deploy of <code>logging_audit</code> table still required before the scan can persist findings.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Removed — 2026-08-15: Green floating "Chat with AI" button on every page (RECURRENCE — fix #2 today)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Recurrence tracking:</strong> this is the <strong>2nd time today (2026-08-15)</strong> this exact problem has been fixed. The redundant green "💬 Chat with AI" button keeps re-appearing on the right edge of every page and has to be removed again. Count so far today: <strong>2</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Symptom:</strong> a green <code>btn-success</code> button labeled "💬 Chat with AI" was fixed to the lower-right corner (<code>position:fixed; bottom:24px; right:24px; z-index:9999</code>) of <em>every</em> page via <code>root/js_load.tt</code>. It only made sense on pages where the chat widget was present; elsewhere it opened a chat window / did nothing useful and cluttered the layout. (First occurrence today's fix was not separately logged — this entry now serves as the running record.)</li>
    <li><strong>Fix:</strong> removed the server-rendered block in <code>root/js_load.tt</code> (the <code>[% IF c.session.user_id && !c.request.uri.match('/ai2/') %]</code> "Chat with AI" anchor). The chat widget itself is still available through the dedicated AI pages; this was purely the redundant global button.</li>
    <li><strong>Root-cause watch:</strong> if this button re-appears a 3rd time, the source is being re-added by another edit to <code>root/js_load.tt</code> (or a stale deploy reverting it) — check <code>git log</code> / deploy drift before re-fixing.</li>
    <li><strong>Note:</strong> the left-side "back-to-top" button (<code>#back-to-top</code>) is unrelated and was left intact.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> no remaining "Chat with AI" fixed button in <code>js_load.tt</code>; the right-edge green button no longer renders on any route.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: LoggingAudit CRITICAL error todo (Controller::Admin::LoggingAudit)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> system error todo <code>logging_audit.run</code> — <code>Can't locate object method "new" via package "Comserv::Util::LoggingAudit"</code> at LoggingAudit.pm:62.</li>
    <li><strong>Root cause:</strong> the controller called <code>Comserv::Util::LoggingAudit-&gt;new-&gt;run_scan($c)</code> (lines 62 &amp; 87) but never <code>use</code>d the class. Perl only autoloads Catalyst Controller/Model/View namespaces — arbitrary <code>Util::*</code> packages must be explicitly loaded, so the class was never compiled and <code>new</code> was undefined.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix:</strong> added <code>use Comserv::Util::LoggingAudit;</code> alongside the existing <code>use Comserv::Util::Logging;</code> at the top of the controller. The Util module (with <code>new</code> + <code>run_scan</code>) and the <code>logging_audit</code> Result class already exist.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>perl -c</code> on the controller passes; grepped that no other caller of <code>LoggingAudit</code> relies on implicit autoload.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: Todo card theme-compliance + Project field (todo_card.tt)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> the open todo card body was unreadable on the dark theme — text showed as light-on-light.</li>
    <li><strong>Root cause:</strong> the open body used Bootstrap's <code>.card</code> (hardcoded white background) and <code>.todo-card-pre</code> used a hardcoded <code>bg-light</code> gray. On a dark theme <code>var(--text-color)</code> becomes light → light text on light background. The card also omitted the attached Project entirely (it showed Site but not Project).</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (root/static/css/todo_shared.css):</strong> added <code>.todo-card.card</code> / <code>.todo-card .card-body</code> / <code>.todo-card-pre</code> / <code>.todo-card .text-muted</code> rules that override Bootstrap's hardcoded colors with theme tokens (<code>--card-bg</code>, <code>--bg-secondary</code>, <code>--text-color</code>, <code>--text-muted-color</code>, <code>--border-color</code>). No inline style, no hardcoded hex.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (root/todo/todo_card.tt):</strong> removed the <code>bg-light</code> class from both <code>.todo-card-pre</code> blocks; added a <strong>Project</strong> field to the open-body grid that renders the project name as a clickable link to <code>/project/details?project_id=&lt;id&gt;</code> (uses the existing <code>Todo-&gt;belongs_to(project)</code> relationship, same pattern as todo/day.tt's conversation links).</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> rendered <code>todo/todo_card.tt</code> through Template Toolkit with a stubbed <code>tc</code> carrying a project — "Project" field + <code>/project/details?project_id=2</code> link + project name all present, <code>bg-light</code> gone, template parses. Both files auto-reload on the running <code>:3001</code> process (no restart).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: Project page <code>todo_card.tt</code> override (root/todo/project.tt + project-cards.css)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> the todo cards on a project page were still unreadable even after the todo_card.tt fix — because <code>root/todo/project.tt</code> carried a ~95-line inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block that hard-coded <code>.card { background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88) }</code> and a white <code>.form-control</code>, plus a <code>!important</code> <code>.bg-light</code>. Inline styles win over the external <code>todo_shared.css</code>, so the card reverted to light-on-light on the dark theme. This also violates the AI-policy rule banning inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;script&gt;</code> in templates.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (root/todo/project.tt):</strong> deleted the entire inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block. The page already loads its sanctioned external stylesheet via the controller's <code>additional_css =&gt; ['/static/css/components/project-cards.css']</code> stash, so no styling was lost.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (root/static/css/components/project-cards.css):</strong> made the base <code>.card</code>/<code>.card-header</code>/<code>.card-body</code>/<code>.card-footer</code> theme-aware — replaced hardcoded <code>rgba(0,0,0,0.03)</code> / <code>#dee2e6</code> with <code>var(--border-color)</code>, <code>var(--bg-secondary)</code>, <code>var(--card-bg)</code>, <code>var(--text-color)</code> (Bootstrap fallbacks preserved). Changed <code>.bg-light</code> from a hardcoded <code>#f8f9fa !important</code> gray to <code>var(--bg-secondary, #f8f9fa) !important</code> so the "Project ID" bar and comments box follow the dark theme. Now <code>todo_card.tt</code> (and the whole project page) render consistently on light and dark themes.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>project.tt</code> parses (TT smoke test); inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> count = 0; no <code>rgba(255,255,255</code> remaining in the template. Remaining hex values in <code>project-cards.css</code> are all inside <code>var(--token, fallback)</code> fallbacks, not primary colors.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: <code>/project/details</code> (projectdetails.tt) wrong-colour text + missing project link</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> on <code>/project/details?project_id=240</code> the text was still the wrong colour after a hard reload and the project link in the embedded todo card was not visible.</li>
    <li><strong>Root cause:</strong> the controller's <code>details</code> action renders <code>root/todo/projectdetails.tt</code>, which carried its OWN ~250-line inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> block hard-coding <code>.project-details { background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9) }</code> (near-opaque white). That white box wrapped the details table AND the embedded todo cards (via ProjectTodosList.tt → todo_card.tt). My transparent theme card/body backgrounds showed the white box behind them, so light <code>--text-color</code> landed on white = unreadable, and the card's project link blended in. Same inline-<code>&lt;style&gt;</code> policy violation as the project.tt case.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix:</strong> extracted the inline block to <code>root/static/css/components/project-details.css</code> and made it theme-aware — <code>.project-details</code> now uses <code>var(--card-bg, var(--bg-secondary, #fff))</code> + <code>var(--text-color)</code>; the details table <code>th/td</code> and the "Total Accumulated Time" <code>h3</code> explicitly set <code>var(--text-color)</code>. Removed the inline <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> from <code>projectdetails.tt</code> and wired the external file via <code>additional_css =&gt; ['/static/css/components/project-details.css?v=' . time()]</code> in the controller's <code>details</code> action (timestamp forces reload).</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>projectdetails.tt</code> parses; no real <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> element remains (only a comment mentioning it); no <code>rgba(255,255,255</code> in the template. Rendered <code>todo_card.tt</code> with <code>tc.project={id:240,name:"Real Project 240"}</code> → <code>/project/details?project_id=240</code> link + project name both present, no <code>bg-light</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: /project/details embedded todo cards still light-on-light (missing todo_shared.css) + v2 inline-script removal</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Trigger (symptom a):</strong> on <code>/project/details?project_id=240</code> the embedded todo cards were still unreadable (light text on light background) even after the prior todo_card.tt / project.tt / projectdetails.tt CSS fixes.</li>
        <li><strong>Root cause:</strong> the controller's <code>details</code> action loaded ONLY <code>project-details.css</code> via <code>additional_css</code> — it did not load <code>todo_shared.css</code>. todo_shared.css holds the <code>.todo-card.card</code> / <code>.todo-card .card-body</code> / <code>.todo-card-pre</code> overrides forcing the embedded todo_card.tt cards to the theme tokens. Without it, the cards fell back to Bootstrap's hardcoded white <code>.card</code> under the dark theme's light <code>--text-color</code> → light-on-light. (The grid page <code>project</code> loads project-cards.css; day/week/month load todo_shared.css inline — but <code>/project/details</code> loaded neither, so the override that fixes this page was never included.)</li>
        <li><strong>Fix (lib/Comserv/Controller/Project.pm, details action):</strong> the <code>additional_css</code> stash now loads both <code>/static/css/todo_shared.css</code> and <code>/static/css/components/project-details.css</code> (timestamped to force reload). project-details.css itself was already theme-safe (no broad <code>.card</code>/<code>a</code>/<code>button</code>/<code>*</code> selector overriding the cards) and is left unchanged — the gap was purely the missing todo_shared.css include.</li>
        <li><strong>v2 JS compliance (root/todo/projectdetails.tt):</strong> removed the raw inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> block (the /ai/project_conversations fetch). The fetch is now delegated in <code>root/static/js/project/project-conversations.js</code> (binds to the existing <code>[data-project-id]</code> container, HTML-escapes titles), loaded via <code>root/js_load.tt</code> on <code>/project/</code> routes (defer, versioned). No inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> remains in any template that includes js_load.tt.</li>
        <li><strong>Project link:</strong> the in-card Project link (todo_card.tt lines 158-160, <code>tc.project</code> → <code>/project/details?project_id=id</code>) was already present and is now visible again because the card body is readable. A "Back to Projects" button and a "Return to Projects List" link already exist on the page; no new link styling was required.</li>
        <li><strong>Verification:</strong> projectdetails.tt parses through Template Toolkit (stub project) — real <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;style&gt;</code> count = 0 (only a comment mentions them), <code>data-project-id="240"</code> present. <code>node --check</code> passes on the new JS. Grep of todo_shared.css / project-details.css / project-cards.css for broad hardcoded-color selectors (<code>a</code>/<code>button</code>/<code>*</code>) → none; all are scoped (e.g. <code>.project-actions button</code>). Live admin render not captured this session (auth-gated) — verify cards + Project link in a browser when an admin session is available.</li>
    </ul>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: Todo detail page Project ID → clickable Project link (root/todo/details.tt)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> on <code>/todo/details?record_id=&lt;id&gt;</code> the "Project ID" row showed only the raw numeric <code>project_id</code> as plain text — no way to jump to the attached project.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (root/todo/details.tt, lines ~187-188):</strong> the <code>&lt;td&gt;</code> now checks the Todo row's existing <code>belongs_to(project)</code> relationship. When <code>record.project</code> resolves, it renders the project name as a clickable link to <code>/project/details?project_id=&lt;id&gt;</code> (<code>[% record.project.name | html %]</code> label, <code>/project/details?project_id=[% record.project.id %]</code> href) — same pattern as <code>todo/day.tt</code>'s conversation→project links and <code>todo_card.tt</code>'s Project field. Falls back to the raw <code>get_column('project_id') || '—'</code> text when no project is attached. Kept the <code>&lt;th&gt;Project ID&lt;/th&gt;</code> label unchanged. No hardcoded hex / inline <code>style=</code> — uses the site's default <code>a</code> styling.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> Extracted the new block into an isolated TT snippet and rendered with a stubbed <code>record.project={id:2,name:"ToDo system"}</code> → output <code>&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="/project/details?project_id=2"&gt;ToDo system&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;</code>, no syntax error. The full-file <code>perl -e Template process</code> aborts only on a Catalyst-only <code>js</code> filter (registered in the app, not a syntax fault in this edit); the link string <code>/project/details?project_id=</code> is confirmed present in <code>details.tt</code>. Remaining raw <code>get_column('project_id')</code> references in the file are the project-filter include (line 98) and the no-project fallback (line 188) — neither is an unlinked display of the value outside the fallback.</li>
    <li><strong>Live check:</strong> blocked this session — the read-only <code>curl</code> reachability probe to the running <code>:3001</code> app required consent and was not authorised, so I could not confirm the rendered link in a live admin session. The edit is limited to the one display row and auto-reloads on the running process; verify in a browser with a project-attached todo when an admin session is available.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Fixed — 2026-08-15: API todo serializer now exposes project name + link (Comserv::Controller::Api::_todo_to_hash)</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> the web detail page now shows the project <em>name</em> as a link, but the API (<code>GET /api/todos</code>) only returned the raw numeric <code>project_id</code> — so an AI-agent caller could not render the same human-readable project or jump to it without a second lookup.</li>
    <li><strong>Fix (lib/Comserv/Controller/Api.pm, <code>_todo_to_hash</code>, ~line 1499):</strong> resolve the same existing <code>belongs_to(project)</code> relationship the web page uses and add two fields to every serialized todo: <code>project_name</code> (<code>$todo-&gt;project-&gt;name</code>, or <code>undef</code> when none) and <code>project_link</code> (<code>/project/details?project_id=&lt;id&gt;</code>, or <code>undef</code>). Now an agent authenticated as a logged-in user sees the identical project name + destination link the browser shows. <code>project_id</code> is retained for backward compatibility.</li>
    <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> the API is the surface AI agents use to "see the application as a logged-in user"; surfacing <code>project_name</code>/<code>project_link</code> lets an agent name and navigate to the attached project without extra calls.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>perl -e 'use Comserv::Controller::Api'</code> compiles cleanly (no syntax error). The change is confined to the serializer; it auto-reloads on the running <code>:3001</code> process. Live JSON output not captured this session (auth-gated curl probe required consent).</li>
</ul>

