<h3>Docs — Planning Language Standard + vocabulary normalization across master plan & planning docs</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>New doc:</strong> <code>root/Documentation/PlanningLanguageStandard.tt</code> — the controlled vocabulary for all plan docs. One word per level: <strong>PROJECT = PLAN</strong> (a <code>projects</code> DB row; the doc is its view), <strong>PHASE = SUB-PROJECT</strong> (<code>parent_id</code>), <strong>STEP = TODO</strong> (<code>todos</code> row), <strong>GATE = done-when</strong>. Retires "Wave", "W0.1/W1.2", "P1/Q4/1A" as structure; defines one required plan-doc skeleton. Owning project #138 PLANNING.</li>
    <li><strong>MASTER_PLAN.tt:</strong> added a "Vocabulary (read this first)" notice; relabelled the planning card from "W5.8 — Planning System cluster" to "Project #138 PLANNING — Planning System (sub-projects: 234/235/236/240)" using phase/project language; added the standard to the Planning nav.</li>
    <li><strong>7 planning docs</strong> refactored to the standard header: 5-field header (Project code · Parent project · Site · Status · Audit date) + a one-line Deliverable + a "follows Planning Language Standard" line + coordinator link to Project #138. Replaced "sub-plan"/"W5.8" wording with "PHASE / sub-project". Docs: <code>DailyPlanSystem.tt</code>, <code>ImplementationPlanTodoAPIAndMasterPlanSync.tt</code>, <code>PlanningQueueRoleVisibilityPlan.md</code>, <code>ProjectsPageFilterSearchPriorityPlan.md</code>, <code>ProjectOwnershipBillingPlan.md</code>, <code>TodoCardUnificationPlan.tt</code>, <code>TodoListPageDisplayTuningPlan.md</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Files:</strong> 1 new + 8 modified under <code>root/Documentation/</code>. Docs-only; no code/SQL changed.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Docs — reconciled Master Plan against the DB projects table (237 projects)</h3>
<ul>
